# Opt-in HERMETIC RUST buck2 overlay — step 2 of retiring the ambient toolchains.
# Flips `toolchains//:rust` from :rust-system (the rustup shim on PATH) to :rust-hermetic,
# whose rustc / rust-std / clippy arrive as sha256-pinned static.rust-lang.org tarballs
# (toolchains//rust:releases.bzl).
#
# WHY: a system toolchain contributes rustc's PATH to the action key, never rustc's CONTENT.
# Change the rustup default or swap the runner image's compiler and every action key stays
# IDENTICAL — so a shared NativeLink CAS serves artifacts built by a different compiler as
# current. Under this overlay the component digests are action-key inputs, so the same swap
# changes the keys. That two-sided property is the measurable business case for making this
# the default.
#
# NEVER merged into the root .buckconfig. Without this file `read_root_config` in
# toolchains/BUCK returns "system" and the default build path is byte-identical to today;
# rollback is simply to stop passing `--config-file`. Same dark-wiring contract as the
# ADR-0560 cache overlays in this directory.
#
# Carries NO cache, identity, or execution-platform wiring: it composes with
# warm-cache-{rw,ro}.buckconfig rather than replacing either of them.

[oya_toolchain]
  rust = hermetic
